    <string name="info_message">ReqLab sends the HTTP requests you write to the servers you choose, including servers on your LAN.\n\nOnly http and https are allowed. TLS certificates are always validated and there is no way to turn that off, so self-signed certificates are refused.\n\nSaved requests, environments and the working draft are encrypted on this phone with a key held in Android Keystore. History is encrypted the same way and never stores bodies, auth values, or Authorization and Cookie headers.\n\nResponses are shown as plain text, never as a web page, and bodies are cut at 2 MiB.\n\nScreenshots and the Recents preview are blocked on every screen because requests and responses can hold secrets.\n\nThere are no ads, analytics, accounts or logs.</string>

